                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f274dbf4-3195-4f24-ba9f-10341e5a6ec9",
                        "source_entry_id": "5914fed9-56c2-32b4-84c5-fa4c13ccc353",
                        "source_sense_id": "936c31a2-1669-3bde-9d27-35bc6c73790f",
                        "target_lang_word": "substantive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "substantive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "311ba9ef-c051-3b55-b278-df21f0fa1941",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the essence or essential element of a thing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af3c84ac-8c6b-4ad5-bf5c-37a8e5d26302",
                                                "sense_id": "311ba9ef-c051-3b55-b278-df21f0fa1941",
                                                "text": "substantive information"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db838df0-19db-4e58-acb4-a99bfc3c33af",
                                                "sense_id": "311ba9ef-c051-3b55-b278-df21f0fa1941",
                                                "text": "In one sense the first debate achieved the worst of all worlds: it managed to be technical, even dull, without being substantive or especially honest."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfa1c600-e3db-3532-94fd-8602d5e0538c",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the essence or essential element of a thing.",
                                            "Constituting the substance of content rather than its style, and thus always nontrivial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21fea0b8-728d-4a5c-b071-172109677c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "dfa1c600-e3db-3532-94fd-8602d5e0538c",
                                                "text": "Substantive editing is never trivial, whereas some aspects of copyediting are trivial."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc30474b-79e6-493c-8985-6823d6c85411",
                                                "sense_id": "dfa1c600-e3db-3532-94fd-8602d5e0538c",
                                                "text": "substantive changes made by the lawyers"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a50f742-87cb-3770-8277-ed135f1cb2dc",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having substance; enduring; solid; firm; substantial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3d62f55-bfd4-4d33-849f-5e9c4b630bbb",
                                                "sense_id": "9a50f742-87cb-3770-8277-ed135f1cb2dc",
                                                "text": "Once more then, strength and magnitude are qualities which impress the imagination in a powerful and substantive manner;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f522864c-38f8-3578-b422-bae51770ccc5",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Applying to essential legal principles and rules of right."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8347066-c372-429c-87af-89b2853e5da3",
                                                "sense_id": "f522864c-38f8-3578-b422-bae51770ccc5",
                                                "text": "substantive law"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e25d611-6a05-44b9-94d0-f944e8065b67",
                                                "sense_id": "f522864c-38f8-3578-b422-bae51770ccc5",
                                                "text": "So this test, this whole area of substantive due process, is tricky for some of the reasons you say. That’s been a criticism of the doctrine in general and a criticism of the general notion that we can have rights that the Constitution doesn’t specify, precisely because of the kind of inquiry that it invites judges to undertake."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4cc2e05-93d5-3fbd-89f0-d22f498931cb",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not needing the use of a mordant to be made fast to that which is being dyed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a dye"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7aa1128-a22c-367d-8fad-aaa2ef9fd8b3",
                                        "entry_id": "7781d087-fa6b-344c-9e58-3e7bd82c28d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Depending on itself; independent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
